# continuity — a failed introduction is spent, and the phase carries on
#
# The introduction to the brewer fails its roll. Nothing about the hall changed, so the CONTINUE does
# not close the phase (NarrativeController.ContinueNarrationSegment): the text stays live, and the
# introduction's button is greyed — it was tried, and is not tried twice in a phase, whether it landed
# or not. A failure keeps the noetic pool where it was (no refill), as it did when it closed a phase.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
state

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect FAILURE
expect-verb meet_stranger
expect-no-outcome dialogue_trigger

click button
wait
advance 12 180
state
regions
expect-not after trying to
expect-state actions action 0 verb=meet_stranger state=spent
quit
